1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:01,996
Session recap.

2
00:00:01,996 --> 00:00:03,775
The orb gets a page.

3
00:00:04,425 --> 00:00:07,273
I asked Claude to put the thinking

4
00:00:07,273 --> 00:00:10,121
orb on my site, under experiments.

5
00:00:10,121 --> 00:00:12,299
And make a 15-second reel.

6
00:00:12,299 --> 00:00:13,220
Go all out.

7
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:16,880
About 10 minutes and 53 steps later,

8
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:17,884
it was done.

9
00:00:17,884 --> 00:00:19,640
One commit, 14 files.

10
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:23,154
The reel is drawn frame by frame

11
00:00:23,154 --> 00:00:25,213
by the real orb engine.

12
00:00:25,213 --> 00:00:27,629
Nothing in it is a mock-up.

13
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:30,001
It got its own page:

14
00:00:30,001 --> 00:00:31,378
the reel up top,

15
00:00:31,378 --> 00:00:33,616
a playground you can grab,

16
00:00:33,616 --> 00:00:35,338
and all nine states.

17
00:00:35,988 --> 00:00:37,005
Then it sat.

18
00:00:37,005 --> 00:00:39,547
8 days later I went looking on

19
00:00:39,547 --> 00:00:42,597
quietbands.com, and it wasn't there.

20
00:00:42,597 --> 00:00:44,122
The work was done.

21
00:00:44,122 --> 00:00:46,240
It just never got merged.

22
00:00:46,890 --> 00:00:48,222
So we merged it.

23
00:00:48,222 --> 00:00:50,971
And Claude owned a mistake on the

24
00:00:50,971 --> 00:00:53,719
way in: a 2.6 megabyte sound file

25
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:56,883
that should never have been committed.

26
00:00:56,883 --> 00:00:59,215
Pull request 23 took it out.

27
00:00:59,865 --> 00:01:03,116
Before, the R&D page stopped at Lab

28
00:01:03,116 --> 00:01:03,488
001.

29
00:01:03,488 --> 00:01:05,718
Now Lab 002 sits on top,

30
00:01:05,718 --> 00:01:07,204
with a live orb.

31
00:01:07,854 --> 00:01:09,721
65 of 65 tests passing.

32
00:01:09,721 --> 00:01:12,644
Captions written for four platforms.

33
00:01:12,644 --> 00:01:14,836
Two things are still on me:

34
00:01:14,836 --> 00:01:17,434
the live site, and a real phone.

35
00:01:18,084 --> 00:01:20,829
Lesson: finished isn't shipped until it's merged.
